# Linguist classification marks (#954): keep GitHub's language bar truthful
# where it CAN be. CX itself is not in Linguist's registry yet — every
# .cx/.cxd/.cxs byte is invisible to the bar until the staged submission in
# tooling/linguist/ clears Linguist's adoption criteria; the README's CX
# badge (scripts/lang_stats.cx) is the self-reported number meanwhile.
third_party/** linguist-vendored
docs/** linguist-generated
dist/** linguist-generated
lang/_archived/** linguist-vendored

# V source here is OURS (vlang), not Verilog. `.v` is contested in Linguist
# and its disambiguation heuristic mis-files vcx/ as Verilog — that was the
# 198 KB of phantom "Verilog" #954 measured on the languages API. `V` IS a
# registered Linguist language (type: programming, alias `vlang`,
# language_id 603371597 — registry verified 2026-08-25), so unlike the CX
# lines below this override is LIVE TODAY: an explicit linguist-language
# bypasses the heuristic outright. The repo contains no Verilog,
# SystemVerilog, or VHDL source, so the rule has no false positives, and it
# leaves third_party/v vendored (the vendored/generated gate is applied
# before language classification).
*.v linguist-language=V

# CX's own extensions, staged AHEAD of the Linguist submission in
# tooling/linguist/. These three lines are INERT until CX is merged into
# their languages.yml: an unknown name in linguist-language is dropped and
# normal detection resumes (lazy_blob.rb falls through to `super` when
# `Language.find_by_alias` returns nil), and Linguist's override docs state
# the case outright — a language "not yet mentioned in languages.yml will
# not be included in the language statistics, even if you specify ...
# linguist-language=MyCoolLang linguist-detectable". They sit here so the
# public bar flips to a truthful CX share the moment the submission lands,
# with no follow-up commit and no drift between what we submitted and what
# we claim. .cxd (conformance fixture documents) and .cxs (schemas) count
# as CX alongside .cx, matching the single entry in languages.yml.snippet;
# the explicit linguist-detectable is belt-and-braces — redundant while
# that entry stays `type: programming`, load-bearing if it ever isn't.
*.cx  linguist-language=CX linguist-detectable
*.cxd linguist-language=CX linguist-detectable
*.cxs linguist-language=CX linguist-detectable
